infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Why PFS follows from ephemeral key exchange
  desc TLS 1.2 RSA key transport vs TLS 1.3 mandated ECDHE
  compares
    - label TLS 1.2 RSA key transport
      children
        - label Client encrypts the session secret with the server's long-term public key
        - label Secret is bound to one long-lived RSA keypair
        - label Stolen private key decrypts every recorded past session
        - label No PFS — forward secrecy is optional, off by default
    - label TLS 1.3 ephemeral ECDHE
      children
        - label key_share carries a fresh ECDHE public key, new per connection
        - label Ephemeral private scalars are discarded after the handshake
        - label Stolen long-term key cannot decrypt past sessions
        - label PFS is mandated — the default with zero configuration
theme
  palette #f43f5e #14b8a6
